  "status": "hand",
  "note": "shadcn-ui-blocks.vercel.app 301s to www.shadcn-ui-blocks.com (canonical host of the same site; robots.txt there allows /blocks/). Its sitemap.xml (4,321 locs) lists each block as /blocks/<category>/<group>/<leaf> (3,913 such pages; the category set is application, application-pro, components, ecommerce, ecommerce-pro, marketing, marketing-pro, modern-saas, portfolio, portfolio-pro and the group set has 223 slugs). The registry names are the five path segments could not be built by a pattern (/blocks/{author}/{*}/{name} would make application-pro-a11y-checklist-panel-accessibility, not the slug), so the url is the registry name with its category and group split out: the one rewrite rule turns <category>-<group>-<leaf> into <category>/<group>/<leaf> against the closed category/group vocabularies taken from the sitemap; all 3,903 url-less registry:block names map to a sitemap page (checked offline, /blocks/<joined slug> never exists). The remaining 99 items are registry:item og-image-* entries with no page (and below the default types filter), so they stay url-less."
